# 1. Data Reconciliation Overview
Reconciliation ensures every source record loaded into the pipeline is accounted for across layers—whether
it was successfully cleaned, moved to a rejected table due to data quality issues, or dropped as an exact duplicate.

# The Reconciliation 
Formula$$\text{Bronze Rows} = \text{Clean Rows} + \text{Rejected Rows} + \text{Duplicate Rows}$$

